# Copy this file to .env.openrouter beside openrouterAdvisor.py.
# Do not commit .env.openrouter or share its contents.

# Required: an OpenRouter API key (sk-or-...), not an Anthropic or Local server key.
# This is the only setting read from this file by the current launcher.
# The router reads it as its upstream credential; do not export it as Claude Code authentication.
ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN=YOUR_OPENROUTER_API_KEY

# Fixed in code; these are reference values, not additional .env parameters:
# Messages API URL: https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/messages
# Replacement model: deepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash-1017
# Request timeout: 30 seconds per attempt.
# Retry policy: initial attempt + 3 retries, with 1 second between attempts.
# Recovery cooldown: 30 seconds before a later request checks recovery.
# Failure fallback: saved Claude Plan Sonnet; OpenRouter provider fallback is disabled.
# Opus/Haiku/Fable and unsupported native features retain the Plan route.

# Launch: .\startClaudeOpenRouter.ps1 -Provider OpenRouter
# Existing Claude Plan login is required for this routing mode.
# -LocalMode and -LocalCompat are Local-provider options, not OpenRouter options.
# For a Local server, use .env.local-llm.example instead; this file is not read in Local mode.
